    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "•. PARSONS DAN\nLENGTH OF KEEL\nBREADTH OF REAM\nDIMENSIONS:\n178 FEET\n36 FEET\nEncored amending do and of Congre in che yeas 1950 ly A. Cans in the Clash Offen of the Sumed Coast of Naw Yout\nCLIPPER SHIP \"NIGHTINGALE.\nGetting under weigh off the Battery. New York\nNEW YORK, PUBLISHED BY N. CURRIER, 152 NASSAU STREET\nLITH BY N. CURRIER\nDEPTH OF HOLT\nTONNAGE PER REGISTES\nBUILT BY S. HANSCOM IN 1851",
      "THE PRESIDENT\nSherry Dubonnet Campari Dry Vermouth\nSake\nManhattan Martini\nBloody Mary Soreriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins\nScotch Bourton Canadian\nGin Vodka\nOUR SELECTION OF VINTAGE WiNES\nGreat Wines of Burgundy\nGreat Wines of Bordeau\nChampagne\nCointreau Drambuie Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP Bénédictine and Brandy",
      "SPECIAL\nHORS D'OEUVRE\nCulinary Specialies served from the Cart\nENIREES\nRoast Rach of Lamb-Mint Sauce\n*+####\nBreast of Chichen with Madras Curry Sauce\nRoast Cornish Game Hen stuffed with Wild Rice\n#**680=-z1\nFried Tillt Ha\nLebster Thermidor\nGarden Vegetables\nSeamed Rice\n6 BR\n¡1 z\nPotato Croquettes\nCHEESE\nSelection of Cheese\nDESSERT\nSelection of Tench Pastries\nAmerican Coffee\nSanka Coffee\nFruit Basket\n7*71125\nOrange Peroe Tea\nJapanese Green Tea\n#***\n8***\nPAN AMERiCAN CUiSiNE BY MAXIM'S OF PARis\n•GOOD FOOD IS THE BASIS FOR TRUE\nMAP.\nNESS\"' A. Escoffier\n3271\n0801",
      "CLIPPER SHIP \"NIGHTINGALE\"\nThe front cover of this menu is a reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives clipper ship print.\nCurrier \u0026 Ives, known as the \"Printmakers of America\", graphically preserved the glorious clipper\nship era in a magnificent series of clipper ship prints. This print, one of a series, is being reproduced\nthrough the courtesy of The Mariners Museum, Newport News, Virginia.\nThe clipper ship \"Nightingale\" was named in honor of Jenny Lind, the \"Swedish Nightingale,\"\nwhose golden voice had recently enchanted America. The \"Nichtingale\" was considered one of the\nmost beautiful of all the \"American\" clippers. She was built to be exhibited at the World's Fair\nto be held in London, in 1851, as an example of the magnificent skill and craftsmanship of the\n\"Yankee\" shipbuilders. No expense was spared in her design and construction and she proudly\ncarried a life size carving of the\n\"Swedish Nightingale\" as her ship's figurehead. She started service\ncarrying passengers to and from the Worid's Fair in London and later was used on the Australian\nrun where she established such sailing records as going from Melbourne to New York in 75 days!\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers* of the air. the early clioner ships traveled the lanes of com\nmerce to all the far places of the world.\n.. to Japan\n.. to Australia .\n. and, in the days of the\ngreat gold rush, from America's east coast, around Cape Horn, South America, to California.\nOur current equipment... the Clipper fleet of the Twentieth Century... consists of the fines\ncommercial aircraft ever developed —aircraft that have helped us establish an unparalleled record\nfor safety, speed and service.\n*CLIPPER TRADE MARK-REG US PAT OFFICE_ COPYRIGHT 1966 PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS INd\nLITHO IN USA - 8739-0393\n2001.159.004"
    ],
